   "source": [
    "✅ R-squared (R²)\n",
    "📌 Definition:\n",
    "R-squared tells you how well your model explains the variation in the target variable.\n",
    "\n",
    "📌 In Simple Words:\n",
    "It shows how well your model fits the data.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example: If R² = 0.85, it means 85% of the variation in the output is explained by the input features.\n",
    "\n",
    "📌 Range:\n",
    "0 to 1 (or 0% to 100%)\n",
    "\n",
    "1 means a perfect fit\n",
    "\n",
    "0 means the model explains nothing\n",
    "\n",
    "❌ Limitation:\n",
    "It always increases when you add more features, even if those features are not useful.\n",
    "\n",
    "So, it can give a false impression of a good model.\n",
    "\n",
    "✅ Adjusted R-squared\n",
    "📌 Definition:\n",
    "Adjusted R-squared is a modified version of R² that penalizes the model for adding irrelevant features.\n",
    "\n",
    "📌 Why It’s Better:\n",
    "It takes into account the number of features used in the model.\n",
    "\n",
    "It only increases if a new feature genuinely improves the model.\n",
    "\n",
    "🧠 Example for Better Understanding:\n",
    "Let’s say you’re predicting house prices.\n",
    "\n",
    "Model\tFeatures Used\tR²\tAdjusted R²\n",
    "Model 1\tArea, Bedrooms, Location\t0.85\t0.83\n",
    "Model 2\tAbove + Weather, Day of Week (useless)\t0.87\t0.80 ❌\n",
    "\n",
    "Even though Model 2 has a higher R², its Adjusted R² is lower, showing the extra features didn't actually help.\n",
    "\n",
    "📊 Summary of Differences:\n",
    "Feature\tR-squared\tAdjusted R-squared\n",
    "Measures fit of model\t✅ Yes\t✅ Yes\n",
    "Penalizes extra features\t❌ No\t✅ Yes\n",
    "Increases with all features\t✅ Yes (even if useless)\t❌ Only if feature is useful\n",
    "Trust level\tModerate\t✅ More reliable\n",
    "\n",
    "🎯 Main Purpose:\n",
    "🔹 R-squared helps you understand how much of the data your model explains.\n",
    "🔹 Adjusted R-squared helps you know if the features in your model are actually meaningful or just making the model look better artificially.\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
